  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let the number of sides of the convex polygon be \\( n \\). The sum of the interior angles of an \\( n \\)-sided polygon is given by the formula \\( (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ \\).\n\nStep 2: According to the problem, the sum of all but one of its interior angles is \\( 1070^\\circ \\). Therefore, if we let the missing angle be \\( x \\), then the sum of all interior angles minus this one angle is \\( 1070^\\circ \\). This can be written as:\n\\[ (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ - x = 1070^\\circ \\]\n\nStep 3: Since \\( x \\) is an interior angle of a convex polygon, it must be less than \\( 180^\\circ \\). We can rearrange the equation to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ - 1070^\\circ \\]\nSince \\( x \\) is an interior angle, it must be between \\( 0^\\circ \\) and \\( 180^\\circ \\). Therefore:\n\\[ 0 < (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ - 1070^\\circ < 180^\\circ \\]\n\nStep 4: First, solve the left part of the inequality:\n\\[ 0 < (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ - 1070^\\circ \\]\n\\[ 1070^\\circ < (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\frac{1070^\\circ}{180^\\circ} < n-2 \\]\n\\[ 5.9444 < n-2 \\]\n\\[ 7.9444 < n \\]\nSince \\( n \\) must be an integer, we have:\n\\[ n \\geq 8 \\]\n\nStep 5: Now, solve the right part of the inequality:\n\\[ (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ - 1070^\\circ < 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ < 1250^\\circ \\]\n\\[ n-2 < \\frac{1250^\\circ}{180^\\circ} \\]\n\\[ n-2 < 6.9444 \\]\n\\[ n < 8.9444 \\]\nSince \\( n \\) must be an integer, we have:\n\\[ n \\leq 8 \\]\n\nStep 6: Combining both parts of the inequality, we get:\n\\[ 8 \\leq n \\leq 8 \\]\nTherefore, \\( n = 8 \\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{8}<|im_end|>",
